layout: template.njk
slug: estimate-electricians
title: Estimate form for electricians (free PDF) | Jobchit
description: A free, printable electrician estimate form. Service and panel size, circuits and breakers, wire, devices and fixtures, permit and inspection, wall patching, line items and total, with a line for the customer to sign. No account needed.
heading: Estimate for electricians
sub: Service, panel, circuits, wire and devices on one page, with line items, a total and a line for the customer to sign when they say yes.
tips:
  - Write the existing service size and panel, and say whether the panel has room for the new breakers or needs a sub-panel or upgrade.
  - List each new circuit with its breaker size, wire gauge and type, and what it will power.
  - Count the outlets, switches and fixtures, and say who supplies the fixtures.
  - Say who pulls the permit, whether the fee is included, and who arranges any utility disconnect.
  - Say whether cutting and patching walls or ceilings is included. Put a date the price is good until, and when the customer agrees, have them sign and date it.
